-- Components under `dom` (backend.md §15.3; language.md §11.8; research
-- 36 §2.5, §4.3). A component is called through a function made where the
-- markup is evaluated, so the kind's `p` calls it again only when a prop
-- is not the one it had last time — a pure function given the same props
-- gives the same markup. Children written as markup are one block of a
-- kind of their own, named by the site and the component's node; with no
-- values it is one block, hoisted, so it is the same prop every time.
import Card
import Html exposing (Html)


pub page : { title : String, name : String } → Html msg
page r =
    <main>
        <Card title={r.title}>Welcome, <b>{r.name}</b>!</Card><Card title="static">no values</Card>
    </main>
